//I-A (round-4): the null literal must be accepted where an array-typed
//parameter is expected — `int[] a = null` is legal, so the argument
//flavor must not be stricter than the assignment flavor. The
//binding-distance array-ness guard exempts the null literal.
int TakeArr(int[] a) {
    return 7;
}
int main() {
    return TakeArr(null);
}
